WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.900 line:-3
One of the most fun movements
on Combo Ski is skating.

2
00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:05.500 line:-3
At the same time, it’s
one of the easiest ways,

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.900 line:-3
to learn Combo Ski.

4
00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:11.966 line:-3
It helps you balance forwards and backwards:

5
00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:14.433 line:-3
you skate just as you would on inline skates.

6
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:20.800 line:-3
you can skate downhill, or
on flat terrain, or even,

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.766 line:-3
slightly uphill.

8
00:00:29.166 --> 00:00:32.000 line:-3
When riding downhill, snow
conditions are very important,

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.100 line:-3
the best conditions are normal, soft snow.

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.966 line:-3
Icy surfaces are dangerous and difficult.

11
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.833 line:-3
Riding on ice is almost
impossible for beginners.

12
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:43.100 line:-3
Sturdy winter boots are ideal for
Combo Ski. There is only one rule,

13
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.500 line:-3
They must support the ankle.

14
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.466 line:-3
The higher and stiffer the
boots are, the better.
